The returned discrepancy after step \eqn{j} is
\deqn{\mathrm{KSD}_j
=\left\{\frac{1}{j^2}\sum_{a=1}^j\sum_{b=1}^j
k_{0,p}(x_a,x_b)\right\}^{1/2}.}
Truncation keeps candidates satisfying
\deqn{k_{0,p}(x,x) \le R_j^2.}
